    {
      "apiId": "article",
      "id": "article-body",
      "data": {
        "title": "How we glaze our stoneware",
        "dek": "Every Northwind mug and bowl passes through two firings and three pairs of hands. Here is what happens between the wheel and your kitchen shelf.",
        "categoryLabel": "Ceramics",
        "categoryHref": "/journal/ceramics",
        "publishedAt": "2026-09-18",
        "readingTime": "6 min read",
        "coverCaption": "Bisqueware waiting for its glaze bath in the Portland studio.",
        "body": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Glazing is the step people ask us about most, and the one we rush least. A glaze is a thin layer of glass fused to the clay at 2,264 °F. Get it right and the surface stays food-safe and dishwasher-proof for decades."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "attrs": {
                "level": 2
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Two firings, not one"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Every piece is bisque fired first, to 1,832 °F. That leaves the clay hard enough to handle but porous enough to drink up glaze evenly. Then comes the part that takes practice:"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bulletList",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "listItem",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Wax the foot so the glaze stops 5 mm above the base."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "listItem",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Dip for a slow count of three. Thicker coats pool in the curve of a bowl and turn glossy."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "listItem",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "paragraph",
                      "content": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "text": "Wipe, dry overnight, then load the glaze kiln shelf by shelf."
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "blockquote",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "The kiln always has the last word. We just try to give it a good argument."
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "paragraph",
                  "content": [
                    {
                      "type": "text",
                      "text": "Ingrid Moe, studio lead"
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Our "
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Fjord glaze",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "link",
                      "attrs": {
                        "href": "/collections/fjord"
                      }
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " is reactive, so no two mugs match exactly. That is why we stamp the batch code, such as "
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "FJ-26-09",
                  "marks": [
                    {
                      "type": "code"
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ", on every foot."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "attrs": {
                "level": 2
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Why every mug looks slightly different"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "The same glaze bucket can give three different results depending on where a piece sits in the kiln. Hotter shelves near the burners melt the glaze further, so the speckle spreads and the rim darkens."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "image",
              "attrs": {
                "src": "/demo/article-figure.svg",
                "alt": "Three glazed mugs in blue-grey, oat and slate on a linen cloth",
                "title": "Left to right: Fjord, Oat and Slate, all from kiln batch FJ-26-09."
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "horizontalRule"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "attrs": {
                "level": 2
              },
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "Glaze recipes, by dry weight"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "content": [
                {
                  "type": "tableRow",
                  "content": [
                    {
